REQP-1725#1 Advisory
DSP_Abus_sign_bit_alert  
design_1_i/conv2d_stream_0/inst/fadd_32ns_32ns_32_5_full_dsp_1_U93/conv2d_stream_fadd_32ns_32ns_32_5_full_dsp_1_ip_u/inst/i_synth/ADDSUB_OP.ADDSUB/DSP.OP/DSP48E1_BODY.ALIGN_ADD/DSP2/i_no_versal_es1_workaround.DSP: When using the PreAdder and USE_DPORT is TRUE, the A operand should be restricted to 24 bit two's complement (and sign extended) to avoid over/underflow in the pre-add stage.
